body:
## Pull request overview

This PR aims to prevent an editor-freezing infinite layout loop caused by a circular dependency between a child’s desired size computation and the parent’s dynamic maximum-size cache during GUI layout.

**Changes:**
- Updates `Control::get_bound_desired_size()` to clamp desired size against `get_maximum_size()` instead of `get_combined_maximum_size()`.
- Updates `Label` shaping and `Label::get_desired_size()` to use `get_maximum_size()` instead of `get_combined_maximum_size()` when clamping/wrapping.

### Reviewed changes

Copilot reviewed 2 out of 2 changed files in this pull request and generated 1 comment.

| File | Description |
| ---- | ----------- |
| scene/gui/label.cpp | Switches label wrap/max-width and desired-size clamping away from combined maximum size to avoid circular dependency. |
| scene/gui/control.cpp | Switches desired-size clamping away from combined maximum size to avoid circular dependency. |




<details>
<summary>Suppressed comments (3)</summary>

**scene/gui/label.cpp:154**
* `Label::_shape()` now uses `get_maximum_size().x` to decide whether to wrap with a maximum width, but `Control::get_maximum_size()` does not include `custom_maximum_size` (and most Controls will return the default `(-1, -1)` here). This can disable max-width-based wrapping and break the warning/contract that autowrap labels need a positive *custom* min/max width. Use `get_custom_maximum_size()` (or an equivalent local-only maximum) instead of `get_maximum_size()`.

This issue also appears in the following locations of the same file:
- line 226
- line 1089
```
	float combined_maximum_width = get_maximum_size().x;
	bool wrap_with_max_width = autowrap_mode != TextServer::AUTOWRAP_OFF && combined_maximum_width > 0;
	int maximum_width = -1;
	if (wrap_with_max_width) {
		maximum_width = int(combined_maximum_width - style->get_minimum_size().width);
```
**scene/gui/label.cpp:1093**
* `Label::get_desired_size()` now reads `get_maximum_size()` to clamp and to decide whether a desired size can be computed at all. Since `get_maximum_size()` doesn’t apply `custom_maximum_size`, this will usually be negative and cause `get_desired_size()` to return `Size2()` even when a custom maximum width is set, impacting containers that rely on desired sizes. Clamp against a local maximum width derived from `get_custom_maximum_size()` (excluding parent caches) instead.
```
	Size2 combined_max = get_maximum_size();
	if (combined_max.width < 0) {
		return Size2();
	}

```
**scene/gui/label.cpp:230**
* `Label::_shape_internal()` now uses `get_maximum_size().x`, which ignores `custom_maximum_size` and will typically be `-1` for engine Controls. That can prevent autowrap from using the configured maximum width. Use `get_custom_maximum_size().x` (or a local-only maximum that excludes parent caches) here.
```
	float combined_maximum_width = get_maximum_size().x;
	bool wrap_with_max_width = autowrap_mode != TextServer::AUTOWRAP_OFF && combined_maximum_width > 0;
	int maximum_width = -1;
	if (wrap_with_max_width) {
		maximum_width = int(combined_maximum_width - style->get_minimum_size().width);
```
</details>



